WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Kick, jump, and punch your way to victory in Kung Fu.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:25.660
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game in North America.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.160
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.720
I'm Sam. Joe here.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.540
What's up, Joe? You're changing it up.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.660
Yeah. I was expecting to say, and I'm Joe.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.120
Who would have guessed it?

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.120
Joe not being here.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.460
Okay. It's Kung Fu time.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.720
I hope everybody, you know, is at least a yellow belt.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.860
There's definitely none of us are black belts just looking around this room.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.540
And take one day when I was a kid, I was a black belt.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.580
You were a black belt?

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:58.760
Yeah. But it was like, I feel like looking back on it, it was pretty BS that they can give a black belt to like a 10 year old or an 11 year old.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.220
It's like, yeah, it's not a real black belt.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.380
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.520
Joe, were you being serious?

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.180
I was when I was like in high school, but I haven't.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.000
That was a long time ago.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.080
All right. So we'll have to talk about if these skills translate at all into video games.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.300
To the video games.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:19.380
Specifically the 1985, one of the 17 launch games, Kung Fu Asterisk, as it's sometimes known.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.840
Now, I really tried to do some digging on why it's called Asterisk.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:26.180
Well, it's not, but like why it's there in the corner.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:34.620
And the only thing I could really get a concrete answer on was that the asterisk is there because it's made by Irem on the back is like what it says in the asterisk.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.820
So it's like Kung Fu, but made by Irem Studios, not made by Nintendo.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.100
Not to be confused with any other Kung Fu.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.420
Right, right. Don't be confused with Kung Fu.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:43.360
This is Kung Fu from Irem.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.880
It's not actually the martial art known as Kung Fu.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.760
Right. Now, Irem, we've heard them once before.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:54.080
Does anybody want to take a guess on what other game they made for the NES that launched with it?

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:54.980
I know.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:56.760
I know the answer.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.300
Oh, okay. Well, we all know the answer.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.480
Everybody knows the answer.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:00.900
It's 10-yard fight.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:06.660
And one one thing I noticed was that the the sound in 10-yard fight.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.540
That's like the only sound you hear of just them.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:14.240
The feet moving that one is this is in the background of this.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.140
It's so close. Yeah, it's the same.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.280
It sounds the same. Just the cadence is different.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.300
Yeah, different tone, but it's like the same rhythm.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.120
I think. All right. But before we jump into what this game is about, let's do some initial impressions.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.400
Sean, I had a lot of fun with this game.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.880
It was it was hard, but it wasn't hard to me.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.980
in the same way that our previous game was

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.660
where it just felt cheap and poorly designed.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.220
This was hard because it was designed to be hard

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.120
because it's a really short game

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.420
and there are only two different versions of it

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.760
which I think are slightly different difficulties.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.540
And I think that it felt good for what it was

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.040
and it felt a little like fighting game-y

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.920
even though it wasn't really a fighting game.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:57.900
Sam? Yeah.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.680
First impressions, well,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.040
as someone who read the manual...

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.480
Sam, the manual, Smith.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.040
And it had all these different, not combinations,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.160
but it's like if you go, if you jump and then move forward,

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.360
then you can do moves in the air and stuff.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.460
I'm like, okay, this is kind of cool.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.180
And it just, it did feel really clunky.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.080
I could appreciate it.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.260
It was like a fun beat-em-up game

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.020
and I liked that the moves come out really fast

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:26.200
and really crisp. It was just, it was just really lacking

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.740
and there was just this little bit of clunkiness

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.780
and a couple things that I think just really prevented it

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.040
from being really fun off the bat.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:35.900
Right. Joe?

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.860
So yeah, my initial impression,

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.240
I felt like it had a really good rhythm, I guess.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.980
It was very, kind of like Sam said,

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.740
the moves came out fast, they were really crisp.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.820
And it was pretty simple.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.380
That was my initial impression

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.120
because it does get a little weird later in the game.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.380
But level one's pretty simple.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.180
You know, you're just fighting guys that are coming at you.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.960
Joe, Joe, that's floor one?

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.980
Sorry, level one, that was,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.480
that was, what am I thinking?

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:01.460
Did I even play this game?

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:04.760
Floor one was pretty simple.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.780
So my initial impression was pretty positive.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.860
Yeah, and I think that this game,

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.560
it oozes a lot of style.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.300
When I first booted it up and said like,

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.200
oh, this is a launch game,

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.100
it was kind of a little advanced in other areas

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.900
that the other NES launch games weren't.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.600
We didn't have a beat-em-up yet.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.200
This was the first of that kind.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.580
And also, just like,

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.400
one underappreciated thing

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.740
that wasn't in my first impressions,

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.380
but just something I kind of noticed along the way,

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.560
was you can go forward and backwards,

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.400
which is something that even, you know,

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.440
soon-to-be-reviewed Super Mario Bros.,

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.900
you can't do. You don't get to go backwards in that game.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.360
So it's kind of cool that you have like this

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:43.860
roam through the level.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.240
It's strange that like, you go left.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.620
Yeah, you start going left.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.780
It's a really weird feeling.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.980
But in Japan...

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:52.780
But on the second floor, you go right.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.600
It's like... I'm just saying like, yeah, but...

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.800
It's almost like you're zigzagging.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.140
Yeah, you're zigzagging for sure.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.120
Okay, so I'm going to talk a little bit

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.680
about the objective of the game

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.180
because we mentioned it's a beat-em-up,

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.300
but this time has like a little bit of a story to it,

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:07.260
which is kind of fun.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.000
You don't really find out

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.440
until like you get through the second floor

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.000
that there's a story at all.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:17.060
Unless you read the manual. In such case, you find out all about Thomas and Sylvia.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.980
Yeah. This is the end of Thomas.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.260
Yeah, you have to save Sylvia from Mr.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.280
X. A very mysterious guy for sure,

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.860
but he has a pretty evil laugh.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.160
That's pretty crazy.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.500
This game has voice acting.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.680
Yeah, I liked that.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:31.960
Yeah. Except...

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.020
That reminded me of Final Fantasy VI.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.480
That famous...

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.820
That famous weird laugh in there.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.280
Yeah, it did sound...

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.840
It definitely sounded like ahead of its time

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.060
to have voice acting,

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.440
but I think we can kind of break this down

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.640
like on a floor-by-floor way.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.760
I think that's like a cool way of talking about the...

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:51.820
Yeah. Talking about the game.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.780
So, let's just go floor one.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.200
If I could start. Yeah.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.440
So, the most common enemy,

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.600
and I think it's pretty...

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.640
It saturates floor one.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.120
The pink and...

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.380
Was it green? I don't know.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.580
It wasn't green. Green is the mini-guys.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.500
Yeah, so... What are we going to call those?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.260
Little people? I think they're called the...

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.620
I think mini-guys is good. I call them the snugglers.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.700
Yeah, the snugglers. Because they really just walk up to you

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.220
and they just kind of hug you.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:33.240
And then they'll form like a conga line on you.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.200
And it looks ridiculous.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:36.720
It does look ridiculous.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.040
Right. They don't attack.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.100
They just... Your health just drains.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.380
I like that they hold their hand up.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.700
As they get close to you,

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.140
they hold their hands up

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.320
like they're going to karate chop you

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:46.580
and then they hug you.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.520
So, right off the bat,

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.580
it's got a really weird feeling to it

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.740
because I'm not... Like, I get that they're trying to, like,

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:54.680
wrestle you down.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.620
Like, that's... I think that's what they were trying to get with that.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.100
But it just looks really silly.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:01.820
This thought never occurred to me

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.400
when I was playing the game. Like, it's so true.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.800
It's crazy to think about.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.640
You have to, if you're hearing this right now

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:07.680
and thinking we're making it up,

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.700
you have to play the game

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.680
because that's exactly what happens.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.360
Three guys will be, like,

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.200
pretty much, like, you know,

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.200
touching each other,

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.080
like, hugging them, hugging you.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.280
Can we make the icon for this episode

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:20.140
of the conga line?

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:21.760
I think we need to. I think so, too.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:23.400
Yeah, I think that will be the thumbnail.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.120
But what's crazy about that

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.540
is then immediately after that,

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.720
you're like, oh, that's kind of weird.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:29.980
That's how enemies behave in this game.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.180
And it's like, no, because there's a guy who's about to throw knives everywhere.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:36.780
Like, yeah. And that's the first real threat in the game.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:40.900
Yeah. And they just keep throwing the huggers at you.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.920
And then you get, like, you get a boss.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:47.960
And I actually, I think I died many times

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:49.420
before I even got to the boss,

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.520
which is why I initially felt like.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.580
And then once you finally do get to the boss,

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:53.640
he messes you up.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.500
Oh, yeah, he'll mess you up.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:55.880
This is the sword guy, right?

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.800
That's the sword guy. Right.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.620
And I really like that sword guy.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.640
There was a good feeling of, like,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.960
evenly matched once you kind of, like,

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.200
there's kind of like, is he going to duck?

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.580
Yeah, it definitely feels like a duel.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:08.700
He feels as powerful as you.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.660
Yeah, so it feels very, like, one-on-one.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.300
I did think, I don't know,

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:16.460
because you just, your guy doesn't move very fast.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.600
And his moves don't reach very far either.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.860
Yeah, okay, so I think we should talk about that

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.760
before we move on too far,

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:25.960
is just, like, talking about, like,

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.240
how you fight

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.480
before we talk about how, like,

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.420
the other people fight. So I think, like, you know,

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.340
you do have an impressive amount of moves here.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.420
You've got your, you know,

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.900
your punch, your crouch punch,

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.540
your kick, your low kick.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.580
You can punch and kick in the air.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:40.380
So you have a lot of options here.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.100
But I personally found the hitbox

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.340
to be a little weird here.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.940
Sometimes if I hit really early,

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.460
it would connect. Other times if I hit really late,

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.700
you know, like, even though technically I'm seeing,

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.520
I'm touching them, it would just kind of, like,

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.480
clip through them and they would be able to hug me.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.280
What was everybody else's feeling?

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.200
Did you find that once you were being hugged,

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.680
you could only get them off you

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.820
by ducking and striking?

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.820
Like, whenever I tried to punch on standing.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:04.980
In the manual, it says.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.580
Just a button mash. Yeah, it says a button mash.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.180
But it doesn't use that.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.440
Oh, really? Yeah, it doesn't use that word.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:13.300
Yeah. Yeah, no, but that's what I was doing too.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:14.500
I was mashing the buttons.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:16.760
And I found that that shakes them off pretty fast.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.360
Yeah. They kind of crumple after that.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.360
But going back to your question

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.480
about how we felt about the controls,

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.900
the hitboxes and reactivity of them,

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:26.740
I found that, like,

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.780
they weren't where I would intuit them to be.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.460
Like, my punch didn't have the range

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.340
that I thought it did,

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.760
and my kick didn't have the range

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.120
that I originally thought it did.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.560
But once I punched and kicked a few guys,

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.920
then I was able to adapt.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.100
I really, I feel like I didn't,

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.020
it didn't matter which one you did.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.920
I don't know if one did more damage

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.540
than the other one, or whatever.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.160
I think punch has a lower range.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:52.800
Punch has a lower range.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.320
Yeah, that was the only difference I noticed

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:58.000
was the distance, but I could tell a punch did the same amount of damage

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.180
as a kick. So I would just low kick for most of it,

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.420
just because I felt like that.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:02.520
I thought low kick was just like

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:03.820
a stylish way of doing it.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.040
Like, I really enjoyed the satisfaction of,

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:07.060
I rarely punched.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.380
I was kicking people everywhere.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.600
I tried the jumping moves also,

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.700
and I feel like there's no situation

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.020
where that is any good.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.780
Well, the thing that was driving me

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.000
to play in a certain way,

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:22.640
and it's funny that we would talk about

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.700
how we didn't really pay attention to scores,

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:27.320
but in this game, the score is important

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:31.100
because you get a very important one-up

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.860
once you hit 50,000.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:38.080
And if you kill enemies with certain moves,

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.320
you get more points.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.280
So if you punch a regular hugger,

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.160
you get 200 instead of the 100 you get with the kick,

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.620
which I think is an interesting way

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.420
to make you balance,

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:51.420
like, am I trying to rack up my score

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.360
or am I trying to play safe

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:57.520
with a way that I think is more conservative?

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.240
Yeah, and that's a very good point there, Sean,

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.660
about, like, you definitely want the one-up,

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:04.720
and, like, that's something where it's like,

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.800
you know, we don't think about it anymore, really,

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:08.080
lives in video games,

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.100
but in this one, it's short enough

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.080
to kind of justify lives, right?

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:13.420
Like, it's not like, you know,

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.420
I have to get to world 8-4,

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:16.840
and then it's like, oh, no, if I die here,

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.300
I have to start all the way back in 1-1.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.080
It's like, there's only five floors,

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:22.160
but I need these lives to make sure that, like,

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.000
by the time I get to floor four

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.600
and I'm facing the Black Magician,

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:27.320
it's like, I gotta make sure I have lives

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:28.460
ready to take him down.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.460
Exactly, and getting past all those frickin' moths.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:34.660
Yes, yes. Okay, so, we're kind of,

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:35.840
we got through floor one,

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.260
you defeat the sword guy,

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.500
who we all kind of agree is, like,

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:39.720
a good starter villain,

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:41.720
and then you get to floor two,

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.180
and things just get, like, mythical,

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:46.100
they get ridiculous, like...

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:47.740
Stuff's falling from the ceiling,

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:49.700
you got eggs that are hatching in front of you,

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:51.460
and then a dragon pops out of the egg,

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.020
and it breathes fire at you.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.560
And the fire does a lot of damage.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.700
Yeah. Yeah, you gotta crouch before it gets you,

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:59.260
or you can just try and run by him

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:01.460
before it gets that thing out there.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.900
And the little snake guys, can you do anything?

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:05.260
Do you have to jump over them? You have to jump over them.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.640
Yeah, because I tried low-taking them,

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:07.680
and they just...

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:08.900
They go through my foot.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:12.060
I want to believe that it was, like,

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:14.140
just a coding error,

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:15.620
but the snake shouldn't,

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:17.440
it should not do that much damage.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.320
Yeah. Yeah, it was, like, half damage.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:21.920
Yeah. Yeah, the snakes,

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.660
really everything on the second floor

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.160
kind of was, like, a shock from...

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.200
Like, what is this building

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.980
where the first floor has regular, like,

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:32.200
regular, I don't know, hugging people,

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:34.440
knife throwers, and people with swords,

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.280
and the second floor has snakes, dragons, bombs,

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.780
and then, like, tiny ninjas that tumble over you.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:43.020
So I was very shocked by...

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:44.800
The combination of the three, too,

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.360
is also, like, a little ridiculous.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.860
Like, you have the snakes,

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:50.000
the dragons, and these, like, bomb things,

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:51.940
and to avoid one of them

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.860
usually winds up with you

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:55.940
getting hit by another one of the other things.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.540
Like, Sean was watching me play very poorly

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.280
as I continued to try to, like,

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:01.840
dodge my way out of a snake

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.100
only to be hit by one of the pellets of the bomb

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.760
or try to jump over the dragon

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.200
and then a snake egg hatches

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.400
and the snake runs right through me.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.320
And then you'll get past all of that

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.800
and then a pot with a snake in it

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:14.920
will just hit your head.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.100
Yeah, and there are those things

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.960
that shoot the three little projectiles

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:20.800
and you have to kind of get between them.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.460
Like, those are very difficult to avoid.

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:25.160
And I feel like just coming from the first floor

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.580
where you kind of go into it

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:29.480
and you're thinking, like, okay, I got all these guys,

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:30.620
I got people that hug me,

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.140
I got people that throw knives at me,

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.060
and I got this sword guy.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.520
And then you go to the next level

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:36.440
and it's just, like,

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.400
you're just not prepared for it

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.900
and then you have to do the whole thing over again.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.180
Like, none of that's there anymore.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:43.880
Luckily, it's only half of that floor

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:47.920
and then it gets a little bit more standard.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:50.200
But then you got the boomerang guy

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.260
at the end of there. Right, but we also get introduced

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.540
to the little people. Can't forget the little guys.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.100
The little people are very strange.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.520
And every once in a while,

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.860
one of those little guys will jump and tumble over you

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.260
and then they just keep going.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:03.080
It's like they were just trying to get past you.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:03.960
They didn't want to fight you.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.560
They just go off the screen.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:06.840
I never really thought about that.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.700
I guess they, do they have no ill will

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.020
towards the player character?

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.800
Maybe they're trying to be. Yeah, I think we were just making an assumption.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.560
We were like, oh, there's an enemy and we just kill them

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:17.140
and it turns out they were just walking by.

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:18.720
Maybe they're trying to escape.

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:20.660
And I think one of the people

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:21.780
who are there too.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.660
You kind of look like those other guys.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:27.140
Yeah. I do think that's funny though.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.100
I noticed that too. Like, if you're crouching,

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.160
they'll jump over you.

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:31.900
But I just feel like

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.760
they weren't programmed properly.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.260
Like, they probably wanted them

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:36.220
to jump over you

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:37.340
and then surprise you.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.600
But they definitely surprised me

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.680
when they jumped over me.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.440
Okay, so yeah,

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.480
you get to the boomerang guy

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.760
and I think he's a little easier

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:46.040
than the sword guy. I think so.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:47.460
He could have been the first floor boss.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.340
Yeah, I think that the sword bosses

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:51.400
I still, I think were maybe my favorite boss.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:52.640
Yeah, because I think

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.980
the best, again,

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:56.820
I kind of called it a duel earlier,

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.660
but it basically brings

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.620
like the name of the game,

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:02.980
Kung Fu, where you're sort of like

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:03.940
feeling out your opponent

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.820
more to the forefront.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.380
Whereas, I think when you're

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:11.740
skipping ahead a bit

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:12.720
into like the third floor,

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:14.840
you and you're fighting

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.660
that big, like the giant

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:18.320
with like the big punch.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:19.400
I like to call him

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.960
the big man. The big man.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.440
Okay, sorry, giant is that a

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.440
derogatory term.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.140
But yeah, you're not really

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:28.640
like sizing each other up.

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:31.180
Obviously, there is an objective

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.220
difference in size

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.680
and you're really just looking like,

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:34.960
okay, should I punch low

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.500
or should I? Right.

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.260
And I felt like just a few

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.240
quick crouch kicks

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.300
killed him pretty easily

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:41.400
compared to the guy

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.840
on the first level where you had to really,

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.380
it was like, is he going to crouch

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.580
when I crouch and then I'm dead?

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.100
Yeah. One thing that I was kind of

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:49.400
surprised at

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.880
with the first boss anyway

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.420
was you go through

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.480
and it's like a mad dash

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.720
across the first level,

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.340
I feel. And then you get to the boss

00:15:58.340 --> 00:15:59.320
and you kind of have to wait

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:00.580
and be a little bit more patient

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:01.480
with him,

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.140
which I thought in the moment,

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:04.460
I thought, oh, this is kind of cool.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.180
It's kind of like you really do have to

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.060
or your enemy,

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:09.120
you consider your opponent

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.060
almost like real Kung Fu.

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:12.540
Yeah. But not

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.440
because of the asterisk.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.760
Right. But yeah,

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:19.420
I thought that was I thought that was interesting

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:20.980
that it does require you

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:22.200
to kind of be patient,

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.440
which is not what I want

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.200
to do at the time. But also,

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:26.600
I feel like that's because your character is also

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:27.660
really slow. So.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:28.980
So you're making your way

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.120
to floor three now.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.260
And I know we kind of

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.280
talked about the big man

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.100
a little bit.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:35.500
I know his name is actually

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.860
pretty similar in the manual.

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:38.100
I don't know if you remember, Sam,

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:39.440
but his name is kind of

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:41.000
similar to that. That's why I was kind of like

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.160
I call him the big man.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:43.160
And then when I look at the manual, I was like,

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:44.280
not that far off.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.060
I'll put in the show notes.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:46.960
I'll put in the show notes,

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:51.160
whatever he really is. But they also they run faster

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.600
in floor three.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:53.780
Did you notice that? The huggers,

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:55.120
they kind of move

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:56.420
a little faster towards you.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:58.440
I didn't notice that either. And there's definitely

00:16:58.440 --> 00:16:59.780
more of them. They're showing up

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:00.640
more frequently now.

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:03.000
Knife guy, always up to his surprises.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:04.860
If you crouch, he's throwing down

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:05.740
his feet knives

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:07.040
instead of his hand knives.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:10.860
Can I, can I mention

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.000
one thing that I noticed

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.480
at the very beginning of the third level

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:14.400
or the third floor

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.240
is,

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.360
so there's just suddenly

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.180
like a plot. If you didn't read the manual,

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:21.680
which I didn't, the first two floors

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.060
are just like, oh, you're fighting people.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.240
And then the third floor just says,

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:25.720
save Sylvia from Mr.

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.000
X at the beginning.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.400
And I was like, wait, are there characters

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.680
in this game? Who's Sylvia?

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:31.540
Who's Mr. X?

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:34.140
Joe, why can't we just do it?

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:35.600
Thomas is right there.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:36.940
Sylvia is tied up.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.600
Mr. X is just text.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.000
Yeah, it's a very strange placement.

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:42.940
From the beginning, from the beginning

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.580
of level three, I thought Mr.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.520
X was the big man

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:47.980
because he was in the level

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:48.800
that they mentioned Mr.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.140
X. Joe, come on.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:53.580
So I looked up

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:56.160
the name of the big man.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.020
Okay. It is Giant.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:17:59.420
Giant is his name?

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.340
I was right. His name is just Giant.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:03.040
Aw, man, I thought it was

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.260
Giant Man or something.

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:06.240
I think he's still Mr.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.040
X. I think that's like a hidden layer of story

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.700
that they don't explicitly state.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:10.880
I think we have to get there,

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.520
though, because we'll talk about

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.520
Mr. X in a little bit.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:15.580
He's floor five. If we're going to just move on

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.100
real fast to floor four

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:18.160
where all of a sudden

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.020
it's like somebody spilled honey

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:21.040
all over the place.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:24.940
Everybody's dead in this room

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:27.080
because these moths,

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.460
I think they're more moths

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.320
than bees or wasps,

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:35.220
have just overrun the place

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:37.220
and they are dangerous.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:38.700
And this is probably

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:40.220
the hardest part of the game for me

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.840
because I only got to

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:45.380
our special friend,

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:46.540
the magician.

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:47.740
The black magician.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.160
The black magician once

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.600
and I never got to

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:52.800
the next floor after that.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.460
the floor four.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.820
I'm glad you say that. Was the end for me.

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:58.300
Because floor four

00:18:58.300 --> 00:18:59.340
was also the end for me

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:00.880
and it was that I didn't know he was called

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:02.400
the black magician. I just called him

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:03.820
the unassuming looking guy

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:05.020
that throws fireballs

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.720
and teleports. Not only throws teleports, Joe,

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:10.680
Joe, we're missing a very clear move

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:12.020
that no one else in the game.

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:13.000
I think I know what it is.

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.540
You kick his head off

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.580
and he just regrows it.

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:20.100
Right. I was so bad.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:21.520
I was like, is this a puzzle?

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.020
Am I supposed to kick his head off

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:24.460
a certain number of times?

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:26.220
I had no idea

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.240
how to get past him

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:28.500
and I got to him several times,

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.580
never figured out

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:30.940
what the answer was

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:31.840
to getting past this guy.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.380
So I found out that

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:35.300
if you want to know the answer,

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:36.480
this might be a spoiler.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:37.500
This might be a spoiler

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.460
for other people, but it's worth finding out

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:40.660
because it is kind of frustrating.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.400
He kind of goes around

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:43.900
on the Kung Fu boards

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.740
as the one punch man

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.480
because you have to

